7206	{"artifactId":"LLD-47e2b81827433589-s1","entry":{"id":"review-20c88d9b3cf5067cd7e59e55dc7704e6","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:19:26.470Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Source inspection and conservative evidence-gap normalization address the ISSUE's root cause while retaining demonstrated defects.","evidence":"The approved ISSUE requests checking changed source and treating unproven clauses at low severity. Both dimension prompts currently say 'Reason only over the structured symbol summaries provided'; their gather rules infer missing implementation from absent notes. The proposed source checks and breach/observation distinction directly address these mechanisms. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-47e2b81827433589.json, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/functional-coverage.ts]","action":"Retain source checks for helpers and genuine partial implementations across single and divided paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Both dimensions currently use structured execution, and divided reviews can infer implementation absence from missing notes.","evidence":"modelDimensionAdapter sets execution to mode 'structured'. Adherence says 'A clause or task that requires code and that no note shows implemented is an unimplemented-expectation finding'; functional coverage says 'An FR no note shows realized is a HIGH finding'. codeReviewGather additionally says 'The notes are the whole evidence'. Analyzer results resolved an off-topic documentation directory and reported incomplete graph coverage; these conclusions were corroborated by reading the implementations. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-gather.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/functional-coverage.ts]","action":"Replace these rules consistently with source-grounded adjudication.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The listed change sites completely cover the prompts that must change for source-inspecting divided reviews.","evidence":"The design lists code-review.ts and the two dimensions, but chunkCall in code-review-chunk.ts independently adds 'Reason only over the structured symbol summaries provided.' codeReviewGather in code-review-gather.ts independently adds 'The notes are the whole evidence: a part of the change no note mentions did not bear on this obligation.' Changing dimension framing or execution alone leaves contradictory instructions in generated calls. Reduction instructions also live in the shared gather builder. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-chunk.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-gather.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts]","action":"Explicitly include both shared prompt builders. Specify opt-in-aware chunk, obligation, relation and reduction instructions that remove summary-only/closed-evidence assumptions for these two dimensions while preserving other dimensions. The documented 1:N routing and compatibility prose is sufficient; no additional diagram is necessary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Changed-file/known-FR filters and serial execution are existing invariants that the proposed opt-in can preserve.","evidence":"Both dimension toResult functions filter locations against changedFiles; functionalCoverageSpec also filters unknown expectationRef values against declared FR ids. The adapter applies toResult again when finalizing divided findings. The driver awaits individual calls and routes reviewer sessions through provider.runReviewSession with internalRetry:false. Existing structured execution remains available for specs without the proposed opt-in. [files: src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/functional-coverage.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts]","action":"Keep these mappings and serial driver unchanged, and verify unchanged dimensions through regression tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed tests give regression-sensitive coverage for source-session routing and evidence-gap versus genuine-breach handling.","evidence":"The proposed recording session provider, forced single/divided paths, helper-implemented fixture, missing-note case and retained HIGH breach assertions exercise the defect directly. Existing adherence tests instead explicitly expect 'ONE completeStructured call'; existing functional-coverage tests script completeStructured results and verify filters. Session-routing and LOW-normalization assertions would fail against these current implementations. [files: src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/__tests__/adherence.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/__tests__/functional-coverage.test.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/code-review-gather.test.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/code-review-divided.test.ts]","action":"Update the existing structured-call/schema expectations and add the proposed regressions, including shared generated prompts and relation/reduction roles.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The ac3 mapping proves the ISSUE's required outcome for the four prior HIGH findings.","evidence":"The ISSUE explicitly requires that re-review of b7a68147dcf72034 s4 'no longer raises its four round 2 HIGH findings'. The design's ac3 proving test only 'records disposition of the four prior HIGH findings'; recording unchanged false HIGH findings could satisfy that wording. It also permits documenting unavailable live verification, which is transparent but does not prove the acceptance outcome. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-47e2b81827433589.json, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-47e2b81827433589-s1.json]","action":"Require source-backed dispositions and explicitly assert that the four summary-induced false HIGH findings do not recur. Treat unavailable live verification as outstanding acceptance evidence, not a passing ac3 result.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":1,"low":4,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T10:19:26.470Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
