6547	{"artifactId":"LLD-47e2b81827433589-s1","entry":{"id":"review-f85306c175315831146586bdd663f38a","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:22:35.573Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Source inspection and conservative evidence-gap normalization address the approved ISSUE while retaining genuine defects.","evidence":"The ISSUE requests source access, LOW unverified findings, retention of actual omissions, regressions for both dimensions, and the s4 re-review. The design covers all five, including source-proven partial implementations and explicit outstanding status when live verification is unavailable. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-47e2b81827433589.json, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/functional-coverage.ts]","action":"Implement the source checks and confidence distinction across both single and divided paths as specified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current judges use structured execution over summaries, and divided reviews infer missing implementation from absent notes.","evidence":"modelDimensionAdapter selects mode 'structured'. Both dimension prompts say 'Reason only over the structured symbol summaries provided'. Adherence treats a clause that 'no note shows implemented' as unimplemented; functional coverage says 'An FR no note shows realized is a HIGH finding'. Gather additionally states 'The notes are the whole evidence'. Analyzer returned an off-topic documentation directory with incomplete graph coverage; these conclusions were established through direct implementation reads. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-gather.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/functional-coverage.ts]","action":"Replace all identified summary-only and closed-evidence instructions for the opted-in dimensions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The listed implementation sites cover execution selection, generated prompts, schemas, and result normalization.","evidence":"The adapter supplies one execution object to single calls, chunkCall and codeReviewGather. The chunk builder owns the additional summary-only restriction; gather owns obligation, relation and reduction prompts. Both dimension specs own their judging instructions, schemas and toResult mappings. All are explicitly included. The documented spec-to-calls 1:N relationship, routing direction, ownership and absent-opt-in compatibility adequately describe this internal change; no additional diagram is necessary. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-chunk.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-gather.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/functional-coverage.ts]","action":"Carry the opt-in through the shared builders without changing their defaults; update existing tests that assert structured execution and old schema fields.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing scope filters, serial execution and read-only provider routing can be preserved through the proposed opt-in.","evidence":"Both toResult functions filter changed-file locations; functional coverage also rejects unknown FR references. Divided finalization reapplies toResult. runReviewJob sends one call at a time and routes reviewer sessions through runReviewSession with internalRetry:false. CliProvider restricts Claude to Read/Grep/Glob and Codex to '--sandbox read-only'. The proposal reuses these seams and leaves other dimensions on structured execution. [files: src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/functional-coverage.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/workflow/review/call-limits.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts]","action":"Preserve scope filtering and ordering. Map the existing code-review timeout and silence limits into reviewer-session execution fields and exercise retry/deadline behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed acceptance mapping provides regression-sensitive checks for every criterion.","evidence":"ac1 records session routing and source-read guidance across single/divided roles. ac2 checks helper-implemented behavior omitted from summaries, missing-note and unreadable-source observations, and retained HIGH breaches for both dimensions. Existing tests currently script completeStructured responses and preserve HIGH severity, so routing and normalization assertions discriminate the fix. ac3 explicitly requires updated-runtime dispositions showing the four prior false HIGH findings do not recur; unavailable verification remains outstanding. [files: src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/__tests__/adherence.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/__tests__/functional-coverage.test.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/code-review-gather.test.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/code-review-divided.test.ts, .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-47e2b81827433589.json, docs/standalone/give-code-review-adherence-functional-coverage-E2026102547e2b818/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Implement these proposed tests and update existing structured-only fixtures. Require the recorded s4 re-review before claiming ac3 satisfied; this design review does not establish implementation or live-test success.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T10:22:35.573Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
